  "preamble": "Retraction of the postalveolar fricative [ʃ] to the retroflex [ʂ]. In Polish, Russian and Belarusian the inherited Proto-Slavic *š was originally a soft (palatalized) postalveolar [ʃʲ]. It hardened into the laminal retroflex [ʂ] (Polish sz, Russian and Belarusian ш), which is why these consonants are followed by [ɨ] instead of [i].",
